  "final_response": "I fixed the option parsing in `src/main.c:355` so `--` no longer requires the jq program to already be set — the code path that assigns `program` (or appends to `$ARGS`/input files) is now shared between the \"already past `--`\" case and the \"plain non-option argument\" case, removing the old duplicated logic and the erroneous `usage()` call. I also added a regression test in `tests/shtest` covering `jq -n -- '1+1'`.\n\nI wasn't able to invoke the compiler/test suite in this sandbox (shell commands beyond simple file operations required approval that wasn't available), so I verified correctness by manually tracing the new control flow against the existing `--jsonargs ... -- invalid` regression test and standard usage patterns (`jq FILTER`, `jq FILTER --args ...`, `jq -- FILTER`, `jq FILTER -- file`) — all behave as before except the previously-broken `jq -- FILTER` case, which now works. Please build and run `make check` to confirm before merging."
